making-visible of the authority behind all offices.


\b \u-10179?\u-8907? Confession\b0 
Authority \u8216?not from Himself\u8217? (John 14:10)
Christological fulfillment of the Source\u8211?Coherence figure: perfectly
derived, perfectly obedient authority.




\par\b\fs28 \u167?7. Podcast translation\b0\fs24\par

Core in one sentence: in Shoftim all power \u8212? judge, king, prophet,
priest \u8212? is given by God, and precisely therefore bounded; authority
that cannot test itself is not from Him.
Image: the king who copies out the Torah with his own hand \u8212? the most
powerful man in the land, with the Word on his lap, that his heart may
not be lifted up.
Question to carry: which authority in my life \u8212? including my own \u8212?
still lets itself be tested, and which no longer?

\par\b\fs28 \u167?8. Source accounting\b0\fs24\par


BHS, Deut. 16:18\u8211?21:9 \u8212? checkpoints: tzedek tzedek tirdof
(16:20), the king law (17:18\u8211?20), the prophet test (18:22), tamim
(18:13).

\par BHS, Isa. 52:7 \u8212? checkpoint for the haftarah core.\par

NA28, John 14:9\u8211?10 \u8212? checkpoint for the gospel, marked as
confessional.
Isa. 5:7, Lev. 25:23, Micah 4:4, and John 15:1 \u8212? checkpoints for
the vineyard/life motif, marked confessional/suggestive.
The placement of John 14:9\u8211?20 as gospel reading and the
delimitation Isa. 51:12\u8211?52:12 (third comfort sabbath):
liturgical/redactional given, marked as such.


